# Moving Circles Network

Moving Circles Network is an ISF generator for VDMX6 Plus.
It creates animated circles that move across the screen and automatically draw connecting lines when they are close to each other.

## Main Controls

- Circle Count – sets how many circles are visible
- Neighbour Sensitivity – controls how close circles need to be before lines appear
- Movement Speed – controls animation speed
- Circle Size – sets the size of the circles
- Line Width – sets the thickness of the connecting lines
- Softness – softens the edges of circles and lines
- Opacity – controls the overall transparency

## How it works

The circles move continuously using internally generated motion paths.
Whenever two circles come within the chosen neighbour distance, a line is drawn between them.
This creates a dynamic point-network effect.

## Installation

Copy the file:
Moving_Circles_Network.fs

to:
~/Library/Graphics/ISF/

If the ISF folder does not exist, create it.
Restart VDMX after copying the file.

The generator should then appear in the ISF Sources / Generators section.
You can also drag the .fs file directly into a VDMX Media Bin.
